==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|gladly|lang=enm}}, {{term|gladliche|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|glædlīċe||gladly}}, equivalent to {{suffix|glad|ly|lang=en}}. Compare {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|glædelig||joyful|lang=da}}, {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|gleðilegur||delightful|lang=is}}. More at {{l|en|glad}}, {{l|en|-ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-gladly.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|er|more}}

# In a [[glad]] manner; [[happily]].
#* {{RQ:Brmnghm Gsmr|I|01}}
#*: As a political system democracy seems to me extraordinarily foolish, but I would not go out of my way to protest against it. My servant is, so far as I am concerned, welcome to as many votes as he can get. I would very '''gladly''' make mine over to him if I could.
# [[willingly|Willingly]]; [[certainly]].
#: ''Would you like a beer?''
#: '''''Gladly''', thank you.''

